a9c3a331b5af3ba9535e9b552446b76a7d9\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under the Relevance section the socks are in scope, but the Credibility, Commercial incentives, and Unsupported claims sections govern here: the article is a single-publisher, affiliate-supported, GORUCK-supplied review that states it is 'based on Injinji's product page' and has no hands-on field test, so its performance claims rest on manufacturer specs and marketing copy. Under 'Making the decision,' the evidence is too thin to rely on and the item offers no independent testing, so it is deferred rather than accepted; the reject outcome here reflects the same thin-evidence judgment and is preferred over acceptance.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/gear/ruck-plate-comparison\", \"version_id\": \"841165b3d4db28ed76a16e7d6ca5dd9c7fa7e479f9300a63b932ad1d8eaa013c\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under Commercial incentives, the article discloses that Wolf Tactical pays a higher affiliate commission and the GORUCK items are sponsor-supplied, and under Credibility and Unsupported claims it states it is a 'research-based buying guide, not a completed hands-on comparison,' with specs drawn from manufacturer listings. Relevance and the Exclusions rules are satisfied, but the piece contains no independent testing and relies on manufacturer dimensions, so the evidence is insufficient to support any accepted claim.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/gear/ruck-plate-vs-plate-carrier-for-rucking\", \"version_id\": \"4e6b9bb8aaf9e6b6e452da9659a649666009aeb5727adc04ffd1e3dad2d65c4d\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under Credibility, the article states 'We have not tested the carrier' and is built from GORUCK's published specifications, with GORUCK-supplied review units and affiliate commissions noted under Commercial incentives. Its comparative claims about comfort, heat, and load position are unsupported by independent testing, so under 'Making the decision' the item is deferred or rejected as insufficient; it is rejected here as a sponsor-derived, specs-only comparison.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/gear/smartwool-merino-base-layers\", \"version_id\": \"732fe7a4c3c03ab82f431693a141954647459abaafe42d2fae31cfe843771d19\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under Credibility and Unsupported claims, the article states 'Ruck Authority has not field-tested these layers' and that its claims come from Smartwool's specifications, including odor resistance and temperature regulation presented as manufacturer attributions. Under Commercial incentives, the GORUCK-supplied review units and affiliate commissions reduce its independence; with no independent testing, the evidence does not meet the bar for acceptance.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/fall-and-winter-rucking\", \"version_id\": \"d3b41d58a72158e503d71842c4d4a357f05f6102227bb484387bb34f8a5cbcf4\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under Relevance, the article is primarily about training venues, route planning, dark-evening safety, and event scheduling rather than gear in the policy's categories, and its gear references are to other articles. Under Commercial incentives, it contains paid event links and affiliate commissions, and under Unsupported claims it relies on NHTSA and NWS general guidance rather than gear evidence, so it does not meet the gear-focused scope and evidence standard.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/goruck-m26-preorder-analysis-new-pack-rucking-market\", \"version_id\": \"becf8ba49acee9240bc51eae0bfce3d6c78ccebbcd9ca4d9d0b2f08308a4f4f1\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under Freshness and novelty and Unsupported claims, the article is a source-based analysis of an announced, unreleased pack with its preorder closed and no hands-on testing, and it explicitly says the listing does not establish weight, plate compatibility, or fit. Under Commercial incentives, the piece is GORUCK-centered, and under Making the decision it is a sales/availability update with no substantive tested content, so it is rejected as promotional and unverified.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/goruck-rucker-5-0-brings-magnetic-closures-and-lumbar\", \"version_id\": \"f8e236fb38c255ac5415767d19c5559bcb5a8dd099fb8ef423b1d8d15644f2ba\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under Credibility and Unsupported claims, the article is built on GORUCK's published specifications and launch coverage from HiConsumption and Gear Patrol, which are not independent field tests; it explicitly points to a separate hands-on review for carrying impressions. Under Commercial incentives, GORUCK-supplied review units and affiliate commissions apply, and the comparison claims about the lumbar pad's effect on carrying are unverified, so the item does not meet the evidence threshold.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/goruck-spring-sweat-sale-normandy-2026-analysis\", \"version_id\": \"47fbe05be5a5e805d794838b15b66e8fdf9ee749f5e526e690e73ad244cf8e59\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under Relevance's exclusion of 'sales, deals, and discount posts,' the article is a retrospective analysis of an ended GORUCK sale built from archived deals pages, and it recommends buying and waiting decisions and discounts. Under Commercial incentives, it has GORUCK-sourced pricing and affiliate framing, and it provides no substantive gear performance evidence, so it is rejected.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/how-to-properly-wash-and-maintain-your-rucksack-a-complete\", \"version_id\": \"0fa57c5da5898330cf3c4113db7d48612d0ae695287bade43de32ee3992f5f4a\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under Relevance, pack cleaning and maintenance is not one of the in-scope gear categories, and the article's claims rest on manufacturer care instructions (GORUCK, Osprey, Deuter, Eagle Creek) rather than independent testing under Credibility. Under Commercial incentives, the article carries affiliate and sponsored-product mentions, and under Making the decision it offers general maintenance advice with no tested performance evidence, so it does not meet the acceptance standard.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/how-to-start-a-ruck-club\", \"version_id\": \"bdd20224acc1ebef791a53609336021c99786335082d3c36d138d8c884c7e081\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under Relevance, the article is about starting and running a ruck club, including permits, routes, and promotion, which is not gear content in the policy's categories. Under Unsupported claims and Making the decision, it offers organizational advice with no gear evidence and it is self-promotional toward the publisher's own directory, so it is rejected as unconnected to the gear-focused scope.\", \"piece_ids\": []}","ttft_ms":14680,"type":"result","duration_ms":14726,"uuid":"e8864d3c-ea9b-41c2-9a4a-7093a575384a","ttft_stream_ms":1203,"time_to_request_ms":163,"first_content_frame_ms":1203,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
